  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 421 AM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nMid/upper level troughing lifts northeastward into the Atlantic \nearly next week as ridging builds across the eastern CONUS.\nSouth to southwesterly winds persist through Monday across South \nFlorida before giving way to a light easterly flow by midweek as \nhigh pressure builds at the surface over the western Atlantic. \nConvective initiation is expected to remain primarily sea-breeze \ndriven through the rest of the week, with the highest chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms shifting over the interior and east \ncoast metro areas during the afternoon and evening hours through\nMonday. As easterly wind flow become established heading into the\nmiddle of the week, the highest chances of showers and\nthunderstorms will then focus over the interior and Southwest\nFlorida. While strong thunderstorm development will remain fairly\nlimited through the middle of the week, an abundance of moisture\nwill still remain in place across the region. This will allow for\nheavy downpours with high rainfall rates to continue with the\nstronger storms which could lead to localized flooding over the\nurban and low lying areas. \n\nTemperatures will continue to be hot and muggy through the middle\nof the week, with highs generally rising into the lower 90s across\nmost areas, however, some mid 90s will remain possible over the\ninterior portions of Southwest Florida. Overnight lows will be in\nthe upper 70s along the coasts and low to mid 70s across the \ninterior.",
